cff-version: 1.2.0
title: MonoPLC
message: >-
  If you use this software or refer to the MonoPLC architecture,
  please cite the preprint listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Xiaoxiao
repository-code: "https://github.com/XiaoxiaoZ/MonoPLC"
abstract: >-
  A side-effect-free, event-driven PLC architecture that enforces Monoid
  axioms as architectural constraints, separating deterministic Core Process
  Control from non-real-time Monitoring and Optimization inputs. Implemented
  in TwinCAT 3 (IEC 61131-3 Structured Text) with a Python middleware layer.
keywords:
  - monoid algebra
  - IEC 61131-3
  - PLC architecture
  - algebraic composition
  - effect system
  - TwinCAT
  - industrial automation
license: Apache-2.0
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  status: preprint
  title: >-
    MonoPLC: Monoid Algebra as Architectural Constraints for Integrating
    Non-Real-Time Inputs in IEC 61131-3 PLC Control Systems
  authors:
    - family-names: Zhang
      given-names: Xiaoxiao
  year: 2026
  abstract: >-
    Integrating non-real-time sources such as IoT devices and AI services into
    IEC 61131-3 PLC control loops is a growing challenge in Industry 4.0.
    Current approaches lack algebraic guarantees on how inputs from multiple
    sources are composed at runtime. This paper presents MonoPLC, which
    enforces Monoid axioms (closure, associativity, identity) as architectural
    constraints. The architecture separates Core Process Control from
    Monitoring and Optimization inputs using an Effect Monoid, a Product
    Monoid for independent domain composition, and a Monoid Homomorphism for
    cross-layer consistency. Validation on TwinCAT through mathematical
    analysis, property-based testing, and a case study confirms that the
    axioms hold within IEC 61131-3, new sources require zero modification to
    core logic, source disconnection is handled without per-source conditional
    logic, and cross-layer consistency is preserved.
  keywords:
    - monoid algebra
    - IEC 61131-3
    - PLC architecture
    - algebraic composition
    - effect system
    - M+O integration
  notes: >-
    Preprint, not peer reviewed. Available at
    https://github.com/XiaoxiaoZ/MonoPLC/blob/main/MonoPLC_Complete_Paper_v8.pdf
